groups:
- target: //pi/hitl/harness:e2e_netstack
  group: hitl_e2e
  counts_toward: [PR-13, PR-21, PR-22, PR-26, PR-29, PR-35]
  tags: [PR-13, PR-21, PR-22, PR-26, PR-29, PR-35]
  owner: PR-13
  reason: 'each phase asserts PR-13 flows (BLE discovery, Improv provisioning, LAN ws connect, rename); no phase has an assertion of its own for PR-21/PR-26 (heap), PR-29 (readiness/retry), PR-22 (disconnect) or PR-35 (identity reconcile), so those read UNVERIFIED at hitl until S5 adds real checks'
  cases:
  - path: hitl_e2e::flash_boot
    status: passed
    counts_toward: [PR-13, PR-21, PR-26]
    reason: 'asserts the flashed app boots and serial shows ''[ble] advertising'' (Improv BLE service discoverable): PR-13 ''device provisioning ... discovery''; nothing measures heap headroom (PR-21) or aborts an unsafe workload (PR-26)'
  - path: hitl_e2e::improv_provision
    status: passed
    counts_toward: [PR-13, PR-29]
    reason: 'provisions WiFi over BLE Improv and requires a device URL back: PR-13 ''device provisioning''; no readiness check, retry or repeated provisioning is asserted, which PR-29 needs'
  - path: hitl_e2e::websocket_checks
    status: passed
    counts_toward: [PR-13, PR-22, PR-35]
    reason: 'asserts ws connect, time sync, rename echo and the cert page: PR-13 ''rename ... LAN connection''; build_info/board_caps (PR-35 in the S5 TAGS) can only move once CheckPlan makes them separate cases; nothing exercises a transient disconnect (PR-22)'
